 thomas wayne performed a life-saving  surgery on him many years ago while  bruce watched this scene is directly  from the comics but is also mixed into  the idea from the telltale series that  bruce's parents may have been as corrupt  as falcone themselves the movie plays it  more ambiguous than the game by offering  several different versions of the story  and confirming none of them so it can  cater to fans of both interpretations of  batman's parents  either they were cool people that got  got by some random punk on the street or  they were evil rich criminal men's and  the local crime lords whacked them it's  left vague enough that you can choose  and both versions of it are spun by  biased parties which is a nice touch  alfred would give the waynes the most  charitable reading possible and falcone  is a liar so it's possible that the  truth lies somewhere between both of  their versions of the past the batman  movie does a great job of weaving selena  kyle into the storyline by adapting two  very popular batman comics year one by  frank miller and david mazzakelli and  the long halloween and its sequel by  jeff leb and tim sale in year one selena  kyle as catwoman fights and scratches  mob boss carmine falcone which she also  does in the movie giving him his iconic  scars  and in the long halloween catwoman  suspects carmine falcone is her  biological father which is investigated  much more in the sequel dark victory it  isn't conclusive in the comics but that  tight connection helps justify both  selena and carmine being important  players in the batman i would also say  there are some visual cues to these  comics the letters batman gets from the  riddler in the film are a bit  reminiscent of the clues left by holiday  in the long halloween and there's a  scene of the batman escaping from police  up a flight of stairs that's taken  directly from year one  finally catwoman learning batman's  secret identity was done in the catwoman  comic that was by writer br